Local modifications: exports map repointed from the upstream intx-src condition to direct TypeScript source resolution (types/default -> ./src/...); dist references removed. Upstream test files are not vendored (they import the unvendored @intx/inference-testing and @intx/test-harness test packages). CL-6448: the suspendable-child spawn seam threads the parent child's credentials-backed authorize and MailPartReader (adapters/spawn-child.ts opts credentialWiring/mailPartReader, hoisted above the body resolver in child/run-child.ts), so a tool-bearing body agent gates its tool calls through the same per-step grant snapshot a top-level step does and reads an attachments-only inbound mail's parts instead of throwing; the sidecar still passes both (workflow-substrate-factory.ts bridges CredentialWiring onto upstream's newer native credentialMaterial cell). child/run-child.ts resolves a step's grants entry through findStepGrantsEntry (head collapse: a body step whose own id is absent from a single-step deployment's snapshot resolves to the sole entry). CL-6396: the event-channel envelope, sender, and receiver carry an optional childRunId; run-child stamps spawnInput.childRunId onto body-child events so overlapping turns HMAC-bind the occurrence they belong to. Temporary delta: buildInboundMessageFromMail omits `subject` when the decoded header is empty (a present-but-textless Subject header), since createInboundMessage rejects an empty subject and fails the step; see VENDORED.md's kill condition. Absorbed upstream at this re-vendor: the step-invoker describeReplyFailure/usableAddr rewording, the substrate-mailbox-store nullable-header widening, the supervisor-backed-transport MessageTransportError codes, the control-channel optional from/date/messageId, and the supervisor stored-envelope messageId/date narrowing. Retired at earlier pins: the empty-mail drop (CL-6164) and the action/loop runtime bind (CL-6325).
